You can use an index template as a way to tell OpenSearch how to conﬁgure an index when it's
created. Conﬁgure index templates before creating indexes. Then, when you create an index, it
inherits the settings and mappings from the template. You can apply more than one template to
a single index, so you can specify settings in one template and mappings in another. This strategy
allows one template for common settings across multiple indexes, and separate templates for
more speciﬁc settings and mappings.
The following settings are helpful to conﬁgure in templates:
• Number of primary and replica shards
• Refresh interval (how often to refresh and make recent changes to the index available to search)
• Dynamic mapping control
• Explicit ﬁeld mappings
The following example template contains each of these settings:
{
"index_patterns":[
"index-*"
],
"order": 0,
"settings": {
"index": {
"number_of_shards": 3,
"number_of_replicas": 1,
"refresh_interval": "60s"
}
